WEBVTT

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.023
(swords clanging)

00:00:19.107 --> 00:00:21.860
(jovial shouting)

00:00:23.695 --> 00:00:24.779
Come on.
来吧

00:00:26.531 --> 00:00:28.741
(onlookers shouting)

00:00:30.326 --> 00:00:32.412
(grunting)

00:00:41.129 --> 00:00:43.214
(Edmund laughs)

00:00:43.298 --> 00:00:45.508
(crew cheers, applauds)

00:00:45.592 --> 00:00:47.051
You've grown stronger, my friend.
你强壮多了，我的朋友

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:49.470
Seems I have.
可能是吧

00:00:50.388 --> 00:00:53.224
All right! Back to work!
好了，回去工作

00:00:55.602 --> 00:00:56.811
-Your Highness.
-Oh, thank you.
-陛下
-谢谢

00:00:56.895 --> 00:00:58.688
(bell clanging)
-陛下
-谢谢

00:01:01.649 --> 00:01:06.070
Edmund, do you think if we keep sailing
to the end of the world, we'll just...
如果我们一直航行

00:01:07.197 --> 00:01:08.698
...tip off the edge?
掉进深渊

00:01:08.781 --> 00:01:11.659
EDMUND: Don't worry, Lu,
we're a long way from there.
别担心，露西，那是以后的事

00:01:11.743 --> 00:01:14.370
I see you're still talking nonsense,
the two of you.
你们又在说傻话了，白痴

00:01:16.164 --> 00:01:19.250
-Are you feeling better?
-Yes, no thanks to you.
是的，不劳费心
我这人有钢铁般的意志

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:21.085
It's lucky I have an iron constitution.
是的，不劳费心
我这人有钢铁般的意志

00:01:21.169 --> 00:01:22.587
REEPICHEEP: As effervescent
as ever, I see.
煮熟的鸭子嘴硬

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:24.172
Find your sea legs?
晕船好了没有？

00:01:24.255 --> 00:01:25.548
Never lost them.
我没晕船，只是一时不适应而已

00:01:25.632 --> 00:01:27.634
Simply dealing with the shock of things.
我没晕船，只是一时不适应而已

00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:31.554
Mother says I have an acute disposition,
due to my intelligence.
妈妈说我的素质不是一般的高
而且绝顶聪明

00:01:31.638 --> 00:01:34.182
I don't think he has "a cute" anything.
看不出他有什么聪明之处

00:01:34.265 --> 00:01:36.351
I'll have you know, as soon as we
find civilization,
等到了文明世界我会让你们看个明白

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:40.230
I'm contacting the British Consul.
Have you all arrested for kidnapping.
我正在联络英国领事馆
他们会以绑架罪拘捕你们

00:01:40.313 --> 00:01:41.940
Kidnapping, is it?
绑架，是吗？

00:01:42.023 --> 00:01:44.275
That's funny.
I thought we saved your life.
我们救了你的性命

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:45.735
You held me against my will!
你们违背我的意愿，扣留我

00:01:45.818 --> 00:01:47.946
-Ha!
-Did I?
是吗？

00:01:48.029 --> 00:01:49.989
In, what I must say, are the
most unhygienic quarters.
那下面是世界上最肮脏的地方

00:01:50.073 --> 00:01:51.658
It's like a, it's like a zoo down there!
就像猪窝一样

00:01:51.741 --> 00:01:53.493
He's quite the complainer, isn't he?
他总是这样抱怨个不休吗？

00:01:53.576 --> 00:01:54.994
He's just warming up.
这才刚刚开始

00:01:55.078 --> 00:01:56.996
Land ho!
看到陆地了

00:01:57.080 --> 00:01:58.957
(crew shouting orders)
看到陆地了

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:21.104
The Lone Islands.
前面是孤独岛，那里是狭港

00:02:21.187 --> 00:02:23.064
The port of Narrowhaven.
前面是孤独岛，那里是狭港

00:02:23.147 --> 00:02:26.150
Strange, not a Narnian flag in sight.
奇怪，完全看不到纳尼亚国旗

00:02:27.777 --> 00:02:30.071
But the Lone Islands
have always been Narnia's.
可是，孤独岛历来属于纳尼亚

00:02:31.322 --> 00:02:32.699
(birds calling)

00:02:32.782 --> 00:02:34.242
DRINIAN: Seems suspicious.
好像不太正常

00:02:36.786 --> 00:02:38.079
I say we prepare a landing party.
我建议组织登陆先遣分队

00:02:38.162 --> 00:02:39.789
EDMUND: Drinian?
德里宁？

00:02:40.874 --> 00:02:42.917
Forgive me, Your Majesty,
对不起，陛下

00:02:43.001 --> 00:02:46.087
but the chain of command starts
with King Caspian on this ship.
可是这条船应该由凯斯宾国王发号施令

00:02:48.006 --> 00:02:50.383
-Right.
-CASPIAN: We'll use longboats.
大艇做好准备

00:02:50.466 --> 00:02:52.343
Drinian, pick some men and come ashore.
德里宁，挑选一些人登陆

00:02:52.427 --> 00:02:53.928
-Aye.
-Tavros.
-是
-塔罗斯

00:02:55.388 --> 00:02:59.309
Man the longboats, furl the sail
and prepare to drop anchor.
大艇水手就位，收帆，准备好抛锚

00:02:59.392 --> 00:03:00.685
(crew shouting)
大艇水手就位，收帆，准备好抛锚

00:03:05.815 --> 00:03:07.734
(men grunting)

00:03:14.115 --> 00:03:15.658
REEPICHEEP: Onward!
加把劲，马上就可以开始探险了

00:03:15.742 --> 00:03:17.785
The thrill of the unknown lies ahead.
加把劲，马上就可以开始探险了

00:03:18.620 --> 00:03:20.163
Couldn't this have
waited till the morning?
难道不能等到明天早晨吗？

00:03:21.122 --> 00:03:23.791
There is no honor in turning
away from adventure, lad.
逃避危险可不是什么光彩的事，孩子

00:03:23.875 --> 00:03:25.418
LUCY: Listen.
听

00:03:26.461 --> 00:03:27.712
Where is everyone?
怎么没有一点动静？

00:03:28.755 --> 00:03:30.340
Come on, jelly legs.
来吧，软骨头

00:03:30.423 --> 00:03:32.175
I'm capable of doing it myself.
不用你们我也能上岸

00:03:32.258 --> 00:03:34.969
-Oh! Aah...
-(sighs)
不用你们我也能上岸

00:03:35.053 --> 00:03:37.055
And you're certain he's related by blood?
他和你们真有血缘关系吗？

00:03:48.191 --> 00:03:50.026
(bell tolls)

00:03:50.109 --> 00:03:52.946
(birds fluttering, twittering)

00:04:01.204 --> 00:04:04.207
Reepicheep, stay here with Drinian's men
and secure the place.
雷佩契普
你和德里宁的人留下保护船只

00:04:05.124 --> 00:04:06.376
We'll head on.
我们上岛

00:04:06.459 --> 00:04:09.587
If we don't come back by dawn,
send a party.
如果天亮还不回来
你再派人上去

00:04:09.671 --> 00:04:11.297
Yes, Your Majesty.
是，陛下

00:04:26.437 --> 00:04:28.731
Yeah, looks like nobody's in,
so do you think we should head back?
喂，里面好像没人，我们还是回去吧？

00:04:31.651 --> 00:04:35.405
Do you want to come here
and guard... something?
你在这儿提供掩护，好不好？

00:04:35.488 --> 00:04:36.698
Ah, yes.
好的

00:04:37.907 --> 00:04:41.870
Good idea, cousin.
Very, um... logical.
你真是知人善任

00:04:52.297 --> 00:04:54.007
I've got it. I've got it.
Don't worry.
我懂，放心吧

00:04:59.554 --> 00:05:01.598
(door rumbles, creaks)

00:05:14.235 --> 00:05:15.862
Uh, I'm ready to go when you are.
等你们搞定后
我随时可以走

00:05:25.872 --> 00:05:28.208
LUCY: Who are all these people?
他们是什么人？

00:05:28.291 --> 00:05:30.001
Why have they been crossed out?
为什么被划掉了？

00:05:31.794 --> 00:05:34.881
LUCY: It looks like some kind of fee.
好像有关什么费用

00:05:34.964 --> 00:05:36.508
Slave traders.
是奴隶贩子

00:05:36.591 --> 00:05:38.259
(bell ringing, man yelling)

00:05:41.012 --> 00:05:42.138
Look out!
小心！

00:05:42.764 --> 00:05:43.681
(groans)

00:05:43.765 --> 00:05:45.725
(swords clanging)

00:05:53.608 --> 00:05:55.026
(Eustace screams)

00:05:58.279 --> 00:06:02.784
Unless you want to hear this
one squeal like a girl again,
除非你们还想听到他像女人的尖叫

00:06:02.867 --> 00:06:06.120
I'd say you should drop
your weapons.
否则最好给我…

00:06:06.204 --> 00:06:07.747
-Like a girl?!
-Now!
-谁像女人？
-快点

00:06:07.830 --> 00:06:09.332
(sword clatters onto ground)
-谁像女人？
-快点

00:06:09.415 --> 00:06:10.708
MAN: Put it down.
放下武器

00:06:11.584 --> 00:06:12.752
Eustace.
尤斯塔斯

00:06:13.336 --> 00:06:14.754
Put them in irons.
把他们铐起来

00:06:14.838 --> 00:06:16.464
-Come on.
-Come here, you.
快点，过来吧你

00:06:16.548 --> 00:06:18.716
(groans) Get your hands off me!
你们放开我

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:20.552
Let's take these two to market.
这两个送到奴隶市场

00:06:20.635 --> 00:06:21.636
LUCY: Let go!
放开我

00:06:21.719 --> 00:06:23.137
Send those two to the dungeons.
那两个关进地牢

00:06:23.221 --> 00:06:25.056
Listen to me, you insolent fool!
给我听着，你这无礼的家伙

00:06:25.139 --> 00:06:26.474
I am your king!
我是你的国王

00:06:28.601 --> 00:06:30.061
You're gonna pay for that.
你们会付出代价的

00:06:30.144 --> 00:06:31.396
Actually...
没错

00:06:32.438 --> 00:06:34.274
...someone else is going to pay.
会有人付出代价的

00:06:36.109 --> 00:06:37.610
For all of you.
他们会买走你们

00:06:37.694 --> 00:06:40.822
-LUCY: No! Edmund! Edmund!
-Lucy!
-埃德蒙
-露西

00:06:40.905 --> 00:06:43.324
LUCY (in distance): No! Edmund!
埃德蒙

00:06:49.038 --> 00:06:50.957
(grunts) (grunts)

00:06:52.584 --> 00:06:53.793
You all right?
你还好吗？

00:06:54.711 --> 00:06:56.254
Y-Yeah.
是的

00:06:57.964 --> 00:06:59.382
(grunting)

00:07:00.633 --> 00:07:02.177
MAN: It's hopeless.
毫无意义

00:07:03.261 --> 00:07:05.138
You'll never get out.
你们根本逃不掉

00:07:06.723 --> 00:07:08.266
CASPIAN: Who's there?
你是谁？

00:07:08.349 --> 00:07:09.642
Nobody.
谁也不是

00:07:10.560 --> 00:07:12.353
Just a voice in my head.
谁也不是

